pdata: OTAP values that read back differently from the OTLP they came from
(found by the property tests, ../tests/hegel_props.rs; UPSTREAM_ISSUES.md U-
entry, not proposed upstream: awaiting owner review).

- encode (OTLP -> OTAP): a span's duration was stored only when both times
  were present, and a proto3 time of 0 is absent on the wire, so start 0 /
  end 1 became duration 0. Now `end - start` with an absent time as 0
  (wrapping), as the OTLP message and the Go encoder give.
- views/otap/logs.rs: a typed log body whose value column is missing read as
  Empty. The encoder omits a column whose values all equal the default, so a
  body of int 0 / double 0.0 in a batch with no other such body lost its
  value ("" instead of "0"). Now the type's default, as the attribute view
  (common.rs) and the OTAP -> OTLP decoder read it.
- views/otap/common.rs: the CBOR reader of array / map values had no half-
  precision floats (major type 7, additional info 25). serde_cbor writes the
  shortest exact float, so 0, 1.5, 65504, NaN inside an array or map read as
  null. Now decoded exactly (RFC 8949 §3.3, Appendix D).
- encode/record/attributes.rs: the any-value double column no longer drops
  default values (-0.0 == 0.0, so a column of -0.0 was dropped and read back
  as 0.0). A column of zeros now costs its bytes; metrics' own double
  columns are unchanged.

Upstream's `test_cbor_value_type_matches_decoding` pinned f16 as Empty
("classified but never decoded"); it now expects the value. The upstream
unit tests were not run here (the pdata crate's dev-dependencies are outside
otap-rs's lockfile); tests/hegel_props.rs `regression_otap_*` cover the four
changes through the exporter's flatten.

Go-produced OTAP (otelarrow exporter) never had these shapes: the Go encoder
appends zeros, writes CBOR floats as f64, and always stores the duration.

